Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.

The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.

Task 1: Assert that systemd is being used as the init system.
Description Task 1: Ensure that the playbook only runs on systems using systemd, and display an error message if it doesn't.

Task 2: Get the latest release of the Grafana Loki project from the GitHub API.
Description Task 2: Retrieve the latest release information from the GitHub API and store it in the variable _latest_release. Ensure the request is successful by checking the status code. If the request fails, retry up to 5 times.

Task 3: Set the promtail version to the latest release tag (excluding the 'v' prefix) if it's set to 'latest'.
Description Task 3: When the promtail version is set to 'latest', update the promtail_version variable to the latest release tag.

Task 4: Test if the zip local archive exists in the specified directory.
Description Task 4: Check if a zip archive for the promtail binary exists in the specified local directory. If the directory is not empty, check if the archive exists.

Task 5: Assert that the local binary exists in the specified directory.
Description Task 5: If the local directory is not empty, verify that the promtail binary archive exists in that directory.

Task 6: Get the checksum list for the latest release.
Description Task 6: Retrieve the checksum list for the latest release from the GitHub API and store it in the variable __promtail_checksums.

Task 7: Get the checksum for the specified architecture.
Description Task 7: From the list of checksums, find the one that matches the specified architecture (promtail-linux-<arch>.zip) and store it in the variable __promtail_checksum. This task is only executed if the local directory is empty.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Assert that systemd is being used as the init system
  assert:
    that:
      - ansible_service_mgr == "systemd"
    msg: "This playbook can only run on systems using systemd."

- name: Get the latest release of the Grafana Loki project from the GitHub API
  uri:
    url: https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/loki/releases/latest
    method: GET
    return_content: yes
    status_code: 200
    body_format: json
    timeout: 30
    follow_redirects: yes
    body: {}
  register: _latest_release
  until: _latest_release.status == 200
  retries: 5
  delay: 10

- name: Set the promtail version to the latest release tag if it's set to 'latest'
  set_fact:
    promtail_version: "{{ _latest_release.json.tag_name[1:] }}"
  when: promtail_version == "latest"

- name: Test if the zip local archive exists in the specified directory
  stat:
    path: "{{ promtail_local_dir }}/promtail-linux-{{ promtail_arch }}.zip"
  register: _local_zip

- name: Assert that the local binary exists in the specified directory
  assert:
    that:
      - _local_zip.stat.exists
    msg: "promtail binary archive does not exist in {{ promtail_local_dir }}."
  when: not _local_zip.stat.exists and promtail_local_dir | length > 0

- name: Get the checksum list for the latest release
  uri:
    url: https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/loki/releases/latest
    method: GET
    return_content: yes
    status_code: 200
    body_format: json
    timeout: 30
    follow_redirects: yes
    body: {}
  register: _release
  until: _release.status == 200
  retries: 5
  delay: 10

- name: Get the checksum for the specified architecture
  set_fact:
    __promtail_checksum: "{{ item.sha256 }}"
  loop: "{{ _release.json.assets }}"
  when: not _local_zip.stat.exists and promtail_local_dir | length == 0
  until: __promtail_checksum is defined
  retries: 5
  delay: 10
  no_log: yes


